Purpose
The Fleet New Technology Adviser guides fleet technical staff worldwide towards achieving a high level of maintenance and service standards, and is the know-how leader for ICRC delegations on new transportation technologies.
Accountabilities & Functional responsibilities
Supports users by proposing technical solutions and providing the necessary training;
Centralize all the technical requests and liaise with the delegations to solve the issues;
Communicates with vehicle manufacturer`s technical hubs for technical support when required;
Ensures that ICRC technicians have access to all specialized tools and manufacturer technical websites;
Create technical notes or repair manuals related to technical issues and share them with different stakeholders;
Liaise with the delegations using Renault trucks, proposes & organizes preventive/curative visits with the Renault Diagnostic Tool;
Advises technicians on troubleshooting and repairing both complex electrical and mechanical problems;
Provides the Fleet Management Unit at headquarters with the latest technical manuals needed in the field;
Organizes/outsource Renault truck trainings &other manufacturer technical trainings upon request;
Keep the Diagnostic tools inventory list up to date & make sure all the diagnostic tools are registered,in working condition & updated properly;
Organize/Outsource trainings for mechanics on all the Diagnostic tools available and supervise their usage;
Liaise and guide the delegations in the choice of purchase of diagnostics or specialized tools;
Follows up on the latest technologies in relation to vehicle fleet needs worldwide;
Proposes processes and structural changes related to vehicle service when required;
Assume and organize implementing fleet environmental solutions and future vehicle innovations ( Hybrid/electric/solar).
Professional experience required
